    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1058">

                <pb facs="1153" n="1141" xml:id="pg1141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.01/7–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Naples</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brandt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-06T10:00:00-04:00">July 6, 1944—10
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>313. For Kirk. Your 180, June 13, 3 p.m.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d1058-f1"/> The
                    question of the transfer of further territory to Italian administration as well
                    as the move of the Italian Government to Rome has been referred by the Supreme
                    Allied Commander to the Advisory Council for Italy according to Murphy’s
                    telegram repeated to you as no. 21.<anchor n="84" xml:id="d1058-f2"/> Provided
                    that the safeguards established in the earlier transfer of territory are
                    maintained and that there are no military considerations to the contrary, you
                    are requested to support a recommendation to the SAC that the contemplated
                    transfer be carried out at the earliest possible opportunity.</p>
                <p>Your 323 and 324, July l,<anchor n="85" xml:id="d1058-f3"/> report the action of
                    the Advisory Council with respect to the return of the Italian Government to
                    Rome.</p>
                <p>Sent to Naples, repeated to Algiers for Murphy with reference to his 2171, June
                    29, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
